 ## Background
-The method originates from the extraction of isosurfaces from multi-material CT volumetric data of mechanical parts [S1]. It addresses the limitation that Graph-cut is inherently a binary method and cannot perform multiple cuts to generate more than two subgraphs in polynomial time, as cutting a graph into more than two subgraphs is NP-hard [Dahlhaus et al. 1992, cited in S1]. The approach was developed to efficiently segment mechanical parts with multiple materials by combining fast restricted region growing with precise Graph-cut boundary classification [S1].
